Have you checked Maniac's Ascension Guide
(http://homepage.mac.com/mhjohnson/mag-r342.html), or the "I finally
arrived in Gehennom. Now what?" spoiler
(http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/nethack/endgame.html)?  Maniac's is
more detailed, and comes closest to describing an AK.  And, of course,
everyone's AK is slightly different.  (My favorite bit of paranoia:
never use the up stairs to leave dungeon level 1; quaff a cursed !oGL
instead.  If you don't have the real amulet, you'll bang your head in
the game, which is much better than banging your head on your desk...)

Regardless, the guide I'm working on now doesn't worry about the
ascension run, though I may mention specific parts of it (mainly the
fact that quest artifacts can be stolen, which can be a nasty surprise
if you're not expecting it).  I intend for the guide to be useful to
new players (and players who are new to certain roles), helping them to
decide what roles are appealing to them, and figuring out the different
play styles between the roles--which is most evident in the quests and
quest artifacts.  I've actually always wondered why there isn't already
a guide to the quests...

